values ('b3d7e1a8-5c42-4f09-9b16-2e0a6c4d8f51', 'general-physics', 'General Physics', 'This course teaches introductory physics through the lens of human movement, exercise, sport, rehabilitation, and health-science instrumentation. Students develop fluency with mechanics, fluids, thermal physics, waves, optics, electricity, magnetism, and modern physics while repeatedly applying those ideas to bodies, equipment, environments, and data. The goal is not only to solve physics problems, but to reason like a movement scientist: define the system, model the forces and motion, measure carefully, communicate uncertainty, and translate findings into defensible performance or clinical insight.');

